	(text "You should expect around 30W of power\nfor each amplifier channel into 4 ohms.\nThe idea is that all 4 are driving 4\nspeakers independently, so that you\nget enough power, while each individual\namps is not that powerful.\n\nEverything is designed around 4 ohms\nload. The impedance transformers are\nsupposed to keep that 4 ohms load\nconsistency regardless of actual\nspeaker load you connect it to.\n\nMind that older TDA2050 chips seem to\nbe rated for lower voltages, so that’s\nwhy I picked ±20V supply, because it\nseems I have the older model. Otherwise\nyou could power it from ±24V for more\noutput power, more headroom. Also be aware\nthat TDA2050 is obsolete, no longer\nmanufactured. There are a lot of fakes\nin the market."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345.44 203.454 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8cd8145d-88fd-47c7-91eb-0874c2cc61fe")
	)
	(text "Each cap ≥1.5 A @100 Hz.\nVerify LF frequency derating."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 195.58 254 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9a9e956d-3f4c-4f33-9f85-eff9cca66f4c")
	)
